1. Structured Data - Machine Learning
     1.1 CSV 1.2 Excel 1.3 DB 1.4 JSON
     1.a Supervised ----> Knowing the Target what to predict
            Target Types:
                1.a.1 Regression  ---> Continuous Data
                1.b.2 Classification ---> Categorical Data
                     1.b.2.1 Binary Category ---> Yes or No
                     1.b.2.2 Multi Category ---> setosa or virginica or versicolor
            Feature Types: Columns or Dimensions (Non Target Columns)
                1.c.1 Linear or Non-Linear
                      Linear ---> having relationship between the columns
                      Non-Linear ----> having no relationship among the columns
                1.c.2 Parametric or Non-Parametric
                      Parametric ---> Focusing on both columns and rows
                      Non-Parametric ---> Focusing on Column assumptions and relationships
                1.c.3 Distance Based ---> Calculating relationship by means of distance
                1.c.4 Hyperplane Based ---> Using Support Vectors
                1.c.5 Probability
            1.a.2 Model Types:
            Linear:
                 LinearRegression
                 LogisticRegression
            Non-Linear and Parametric:
                 DecisionTreeClassifier
                 DecisionTreeRegressor
                 RandomForestRegressor (Bagging Principle - Parallel Processing - Ensemble Technique)
                 RandomForestClassifier(Bagging Principle - Parallel Processing - Ensemble Technique)
                 Boosting Algorithm (Boosting Principle - Series Processing - Ensemble Technique)
                     1. XGBoosting
                     2. GradientBoosting
                     3. CatBoosting
                     4. LightGBMBoosting
                 Stacking Algorithm (More than one model at a time)
                     1. Training will be done with different models ,prediction will happen with another
                     model.
            Hyperplane: (Binary Classifier)(Linear)
                 SVM - SVR
                 SVM - SVC
            KNN - Distance Based Algorithm (Non-Linear)
                KNearestClassifier
                KNearestRegressor


